# Test tooling only — fengari (Lua VM) and jsdom, used by tools/*.test.js and
# the NUI checks. NOTHING at runtime imports these: the resource has no build
# step and FiveM never looks in here. Reinstall with `npm i` in this folder.
node_modules/

# NOTE: layout.json is deliberately TRACKED, not ignored.
#
# It is what /hudpublish writes, and it is the shipped HUD: the element offsets
# AND the per-aspect minimap profiles, which between them are the tuning this
# resource is worth installing for. server.lua loads it on start, so shipping
# it is what makes a fresh install look like the screenshots instead of like
# the raw stylesheet. Config.DefaultLayout mirrors the offsets half as the
# /hudreset fallback.
#
# Running /hudpublish on your own server rewrites it, which git will show as a
# modified file. That is expected -- commit it if you want your tuning to be
# the project's default, otherwise leave it dirty or check it out again.

# Per-server popup theme, written by /themepublish. Not tracked: unlike the
# layout there is no shipped design here worth distributing.
theme.json

# Python build tooling leftovers.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Working copies of stream assets. The shipped .ytd files in stream/ ARE
# tracked; this is the pre-conversion original kept next to them by hand.
*.orig-rgbonly

# Editor / OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
